  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under refill protocol RBC-RX-05: 7 original messages plus 1 that arrived while working, all closed.\n\n- Samuel Price (pt-0030): Metformin 1000 mg BID renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0002). Most recent eGFR is 58 (corrected), and the outside HbA1c from 2026-08-19 is within 6 months. This one order covers his portal message and both pharmacy requests. Lisinopril 20 mg was first renewed (mr-t0001). At 08:00 the lab corrected his creatinine to 1.49, which is 35% above the 1.10 before the dose increase, so I cancelled that order before it was dispensed. Urgent review task to you (task-t0022, about mr-00295). Corrected message sent to the patient.\n- Frank Odum (pt-0027): Lisinopril 10 mg was first renewed (mr-t0003) with a repeat BMP ordered (sr-t0006), because the August potassium of 5.9 was on a hemolyzed sample. Then an outside BMP from 10/20 arrived on a good sample with potassium 5.8. I cancelled mr-t0003 before it was dispensed. Urgent review task to you (task-t0023, about mr-00283). Corrected message sent. sr-t0006 is still open for you to adjust.\n- Marcus Webb (pt-0031): Lisinopril 10 mg is a 30-day supply with 0 refills (mr-t0004), and I ordered a BMP (sr-t0007). His last BMP was collected 2025-10-20, outside 12 months, and he had a visit on 2026-09-28. Metformin 500 mg BID renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0005). His most recent eGFR is 92; the 10/14 result was entered in error, so I didn't use it. HbA1c 6.9% on 2026-09-28. A potassium-only result of 4.6 came in today; it doesn't change anything.\n- Leonard Kaplan (pt-0070): Lisinopril 20 mg not refilled. His 10/19 creatinine of 1.46 is 46% above the 1.00 before the 9/28 dose increase. Urgent review task to you (task-t0008, about mr-70002). mr-70002 was left active. Patient told the refill is waiting on your review.\n\nAll patients got replies, and each has a note in the chart. The results queue still has unrelated items for other patients that I didn't touch."